  "limits": [
    "PHP substitutes persistent constants such as NAN and PHP_INT_MAX while compiling; Phego leaves them for execution, so [NAN . ''] lacks its compile warning. Excluded from the fixture and listed in docs/decisions/compatibility-php8512.md.",
    "SPL classes such as ArrayObject have no inheritance metadata before W-29; static covariance cases use equivalent user classes.",
    "Constant expressions fold a class operand before PHP checks it, so const X = (A::class)::C; and const X = (PHP_EOL)::C; compile in PHP but not in Phego.",
    "Closures inside attribute arguments are checked as constant expressions but their bodies are not lowered, so their compile-time diagnostics are missing.",
    "Inheritance errors follow child method order and name the earliest ancestor; PHP follows parent order, reports properties first and names the nearest override. $a[] ??= 1 and multi-line virtual hook lines also differ.",
    "Lower returns only the CompileError on a compile failure, so warnings PHP prints before the fatal error are not available to the caller; W-17 decides the error display path.",
    "A right-nested constant expression deeper than 2,048 levels still reports a host resource limit; PHP compiles it."
  ],
  "verification_note": "Red logs fail by design.",
  "review_status": "All nine PR #129 review comments on 3da26d5 were reproduced with the pinned images and fixed with failing-first regression cases. Independent adversarial reviews of dc2b04f and c98cc07 found regressions and same-pattern gaps, including constant evaluation that rejected long concatenations, 3,000-term logical chains and 70,000-element arrays and probes that took quadratic time; these are fixed with new cases, and the rest are listed in limits."
